From 559a09636a5dc2a68177492209c0b2bee499738b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ejaaskel <esa.jaaskela@suomi24.fi>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:18:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Allow qemu-arm to use a separate device tree

The QEMU arm boards use the device tree QEMU generates at run time
(OF_HAS_PRIOR_STAGE), and the build refuses configurations without
OF_BOARD. Sulka's verified boot reference for qemuarm64 builds the
device tree of the virt machine into U-Boot with OF_SEPARATE instead,
so that the control device tree that carries the FIT signature
verification key is part of U-Boot and not passed by QEMU.

OF_HAS_PRIOR_STAGE has no prompt and ARCH_QEMU implies it, so it cannot
be disabled in a configuration fragment, and the build check fails
without OF_BOARD. At run time it is used by standard boot and the EFI
loader, which Sulka's verified boot configuration disables, and to print
a warning when the device tree is not from a prior stage:

  Warning: Unexpected devicetree source (not from a prior stage)
  Warning: U-Boot may not function properly

The warning is expected with the built-in device tree. Allow the board
in the check.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Sulka qemuarm64 verified boot reference]
Signed-off-by: ejaaskel <esa.jaaskela@suomi24.fi>
---
 scripts/of_allowlist.txt | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/scripts/of_allowlist.txt b/scripts/of_allowlist.txt
index e82cf55..4e1c15a 100644
--- a/scripts/of_allowlist.txt
+++ b/scripts/of_allowlist.txt
@@ -1 +1,2 @@
 # List of boards which are permitted to use OF_HAS_PRIOR_STAGE without OF_BOARD
+qemu-arm
